# Module system

The API uses an auto-discovery pattern so that `{{ app_name }}/src/api.py` stays thin and never needs to be edited when adding new Catala modules.

## How it works

Each file in `{{ app_name }}/src/modules/` that exports a `router` (a FastAPI `APIRouter`) is automatically discovered and included in the application at startup. The `paidleave` module is included as a working example.

## Adding a new module

Create a new file in `{{ app_name }}/src/modules/` — for example, `{{ app_name }}/src/modules/eligibility.py`:

```python
from fastapi import APIRouter

router = APIRouter(prefix="/my-namespace", tags=["eligibility"])

@router.post("/check")
def check_eligibility(...):
    ...
```

That's it — no changes to `api.py` required. The new endpoint will be available at `/my-namespace/check` on the next server start.

## Disabling modules

Set the `DISABLED_MODULES` environment variable to a comma-separated list of module filenames (without `.py`) to prevent them from loading:

```bash
# Disable the demo paidleave module
DISABLED_MODULES=paidleave

# Disable multiple modules
DISABLED_MODULES=paidleave,eligibility
```
